      "number": 7,
      "title": "A Different Smile",
      "content": "📖 Opening Quote\n\"Sometimes the heart notices someone long before the mind is ready to admit it.\"\n\nThe annual Charity Fair transformed Westbridge University into a festival of colors.\n\nStudent clubs lined the walkways with games, food stalls, music, and decorations.\n\nFor one afternoon...\n\nAssignments and deadlines were forgotten.\n\nLaughter filled every corner of the campus.\n\nMarcus stretched his arms.\n\n\"Today...\"\n\n\"I refuse to think about books.\"\n\nLena laughed.\n\n\"You say that every weekend.\"\n\n\"And I mean it every weekend.\"\n\nEthan shook his head.\n\n\"You'll be begging Ariana for notes tomorrow.\"\n\nMarcus pointed at Ariana.\n\n\"She's too kind to refuse.\"\n\nAriana smiled.\n\n\"I really should start charging you.\"\n\nThe group laughed.\n\nThey wandered from stall to stall.\n\nLena won a small teddy bear at a ring-toss game.\n\nMarcus somehow lost three games in a row.\n\n\"I've been cheated,\" he complained.\n\n\"No,\" Chloe teased.\n\n\"You're just terrible.\"\n\nEven Marcus laughed at himself.\n\nNear the center of the fair...\n\nA volunteer approached them.\n\n\"We need two people for the fundraising challenge.\"\n\nBefore anyone could answer...\n\nMarcus pushed Ethan and Ariana forward.\n\n\"I volunteer these two!\"\n\n\"What?\" Ariana exclaimed.\n\nMarcus grinned.\n\n\"You'll survive.\"\n\nThe volunteer smiled.\n\n\"Perfect.\"\n\nFor the next twenty minutes...\n\nAriana and Ethan worked together to complete the challenge.\n\nThey laughed whenever they made mistakes.\n\nCheered each other on.\n\nAnd eventually won first place.\n\nThe crowd applauded as they accepted a small certificate.\n\nWhen they returned...\n\nMarcus folded his arms dramatically.\n\n\"So...\"\n\n\"You two forgot we existed?\"\n\nAriana laughed.\n\n\"It was only twenty minutes.\"\n\nEthan smiled.\n\n\"They're just jealous we won.\"\n\nAs everyone continued talking...\n\nLena leaned toward Chloe.\n\n\"They actually make a good team.\"\n\nChloe glanced at Ethan and Ariana.\n\nThey were laughing over something Marcus had said.\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"They do.\"\n\nThere was no jealousy in her voice.\n\nOnly happiness for her friends.\n\nThat evening...\n\nThe group sat beneath the old oak tree sharing snacks.\n\nThe conversation drifted from exams to dreams.\n\nThen Marcus suddenly asked,\n\n\"So...\"\n\n\"Who here has a crush?\"\n\nLena nearly choked on her drink.\n\n\"Marcus!\"\n\n\"What?\"\n\n\"I'm just asking.\"\n\nAriana laughed.\n\n\"I don't.\"\n\nMarcus looked at Ethan.\n\n\"What about you?\"\n\nEthan hesitated.\n\nFor just a second.\n\nThen smiled.\n\n\"Maybe.\"\n\nMarcus's eyes widened.\n\n\"I knew it!\"\n\n\"Who is she?\"\n\nEthan chuckled.\n\n\"I'm not telling you.\"\n\n\"Aww...\"\n\nMarcus groaned dramatically.\n\n\"You're no fun.\"\n\nThe conversation quickly moved on.\n\nBut Chloe noticed something.\n\nJust for a brief moment...\n\nWhen Ethan smiled...\n\nHis eyes had wandered toward Ariana.\n\nOnly for a second.\n\nThen they were gone.\n\nChloe frowned slightly.\n\nPerhaps...\n\nShe had imagined it.\n\nLater that night...\n\nAs Ariana walked back to her hostel...\n\nEthan caught up with her.\n\n\"You forgot your notebook.\"\n\n\"Oh!\"\n\nShe laughed.\n\n\"Thank you.\"\n\n\"You'd be lost without it.\"\n\n\"I know.\"\n\nThey walked together for a short distance.\n\nBefore parting ways...\n\nEthan smiled.\n\n\"Goodnight, Ari.\"\n\n\"Goodnight.\"\n\nHe watched her disappear into the building.\n\nThen quietly whispered to himself,\n\n\"Sleep well.\"\n\nHe turned and walked away.\n\nUnaware...\n\nThat someone standing in the shadows had seen the entire exchange.\n\nThe figure remained still for a moment.\n\nThen silently walked in the opposite direction.\n\n💭 Ending Quote\n🌙\n\"Some stories begin with love... while others begin with someone quietly watching from a distance.\""
