      "title": "Anonymous",
      "content": "📖 Opening Quote\n\"The most frightening enemies are the ones who know your name... while hiding their own.\"\n\nAriana barely slept.\n\nThe note lay on her desk.\n\nThree simple words.\n\nWE KNOW.\n\nShe read them over and over again.\n\nWho had written them?\n\nAnd how had they gotten into her room?\n\nThe next morning...\n\nShe slipped the note into her backpack and headed to class.\n\nShe had decided not to tell anyone.\n\nNot yet.\n\nPerhaps...\n\nIt was just a cruel prank.\n\nBy lunchtime...\n\nThe Circle of Five gathered beneath the old oak tree.\n\nMarcus noticed Ariana's silence immediately.\n\n\"You've been quiet all morning.\"\n\n\"I'm just tired.\"\n\nLena frowned.\n\n\"You don't look okay.\"\n\n\"I'm fine.\"\n\nEthan wasn't convinced.\n\n\"Ari...\"\n\n\"You know you can tell us anything.\"\n\nFor a moment...\n\nShe almost did.\n\nAlmost.\n\nBut instead...\n\nShe forced a smile.\n\n\"I just need some rest.\"\n\nChloe gently squeezed her shoulder.\n\n\"Don't push yourself too hard.\"\n\n\"We're here if you need us.\"\n\nAriana nodded.\n\n\"I know.\"\n\nLater that afternoon...\n\nShe finally decided to visit Professor Adams.\n\nShe placed the folded note on his desk.\n\n\"I found this in my bag.\"\n\nProfessor Adams carefully unfolded it.\n\nHis expression changed.\n\n\"Did anyone see you receive it?\"\n\n\"No.\"\n\n\"Have you told your friends?\"\n\nAriana shook her head.\n\n\"I didn't want to worry them.\"\n\nProfessor Adams leaned back.\n\n\"This isn't something to ignore.\"\n\n\"I'm informing campus security.\"\n\nWithin the hour...\n\nDaniel Brooks was called into the meeting.\n\nHe picked up the note without saying a word.\n\nAfter a long moment...\n\nHe looked at Ariana.\n\n\"Whoever wrote this...\"\n\n\"Wants you to feel afraid.\"\n\nAriana swallowed.\n\n\"Why me?\"\n\nDaniel didn't answer immediately.\n\nInstead...\n\nHe asked a different question.\n\n\"Miss Cole...\"\n\n\"Can you think of anyone who might want to hurt you?\"\n\nThe question echoed through the room.\n\nAriana searched her memory.\n\nHer classmates.\n\nHer lecturers.\n\nHer friends.\n\nShe slowly shook her head.\n\n\"No.\"\n\n\"I've never had enemies.\"\n\nDaniel nodded thoughtfully.\n\n\"Sometimes...\"\n\n\"The people we least expect are the ones we never think to question.\"\n\nAriana frowned.\n\nShe didn't understand what he meant.\n\nAs evening settled over the campus...\n\nMarcus organized the promised movie night in Ariana's hostel common room.\n\nLena brought popcorn.\n\nEthan arrived with drinks.\n\nChloe carried Ariana's favorite chocolate.\n\nFor two hours...\n\nThe investigation disappeared.\n\nThey laughed.\n\nJoked.\n\nComplained about Marcus talking during the movie.\n\nIt almost felt like everything was normal again.\n\nAlmost.\n\nWhen the movie ended...\n\nThe friends walked Ariana back to her room.\n\n\"Sleep well,\" Lena said.\n\n\"Call us if you need anything,\" Ethan added.\n\nMarcus pointed a finger at her.\n\n\"And no more worrying tonight.\"\n\nChloe smiled warmly.\n\n\"We'll see you tomorrow.\"\n\nAriana watched them disappear down the hallway.\n\nShe smiled.\n\nNo matter what happened...\n\nShe still had her friends.\n\nThat thought gave her comfort.\n\nShe unlocked her room.\n\nStepped inside.\n\nThen froze.\n\nHer desk drawer...\n\nWas open.\n\nShe was certain...\n\nShe had locked it before leaving.\n\nSlowly...\n\nShe walked closer.\n\nEverything looked untouched.\n\nExcept for one thing.\n\nThe anonymous note...\n\nWas gone.\n\n💭 Ending Quote\n\"Sometimes the greatest threat isn't what is left behind... but what silently disappears.\"   🌑"
