      "number": 16,
      "title": "The Missing Minute",
      "content": "📖 Opening Quote\n\"Sometimes one missing minute can hide an entire truth.\"\n\nThe investigation entered its third week.\n\nWestbridge University slowly returned to its routine.\n\nLectures continued.\n\nAssignments were submitted.\n\nStudents laughed in the hallways once again.\n\nBut for Ariana...\n\nNothing felt normal.\n\nEvery whisper still made her wonder if it was about her.\n\nInside the security office...\n\nDaniel watched the CCTV footage for what felt like the hundredth time.\n\nThe digital clock in the corner of the screen moved steadily.\n\n10:41.\n\n10:42.\n\n10:43...\n\nHe frowned.\n\nThe screen suddenly flickered.\n\nWhen the image returned...\n\nThe timestamp read 10:45.\n\nDaniel leaned closer.\n\n\"Pause.\"\n\nThe technician froze the video.\n\n\"What happened to 10:44?\"\n\nThe technician replayed the footage.\n\nAgain.\n\nAnd again.\n\nThe same thing happened.\n\nOne entire minute...\n\nWas missing.\n\n\"Can security cameras lose footage like that?\" Daniel asked.\n\nThe technician shook his head.\n\n\"Not by accident.\"\n\n\"Someone deleted that minute.\"\n\nDaniel's eyes remained fixed on the screen.\n\n\"So whoever planned this...\"\n\n\"Knew exactly what they were doing.\"\n\nMeanwhile...\n\nAriana and her friends were studying in the library.\n\nMarcus dropped his pen.\n\n\"I'm officially giving up.\"\n\nLena smiled.\n\n\"You've said that five times today.\"\n\n\"And I mean it every time.\"\n\nEthan chuckled.\n\n\"You'll still be here in an hour.\"\n\nMarcus sighed dramatically.\n\n\"I hate that you're right.\"\n\nThe table filled with quiet laughter.\n\nFor a little while...\n\nThe investigation felt far away.\n\nAs Ariana packed her books...\n\nShe noticed Chloe staring out the library window.\n\n\"You okay?\"\n\nChloe blinked before smiling.\n\n\"Yeah.\"\n\n\"Just thinking.\"\n\n\"About what?\"\n\n\"Our final year.\"\n\n\"It's gone by so fast.\"\n\nAriana nodded.\n\n\"It really has.\"\n\n\"We should make more memories.\"\n\nChloe smiled.\n\n\"I'd like that.\"\n\nThat evening...\n\nDaniel walked through the Research Archive alone.\n\nThe room had remained sealed since the documents disappeared.\n\nEverything appeared untouched.\n\nBooks neatly arranged.\n\nCabinets locked.\n\nNothing seemed out of place.\n\nAs he turned to leave...\n\nSomething caught his eye.\n\nA tiny scratch...\n\nNear the electronic card reader.\n\nHe crouched down.\n\nThe mark was fresh.\n\nAlmost invisible.\n\nHe gently ran his finger across it.\n\nSomeone had tampered with the scanner.\n\nNot enough for anyone else to notice.\n\nBut enough to install something...\n\nOr remove it.\n\nDaniel stood slowly.\n\nA new thought crossed his mind.\n\n\"What if...\"\n\n\"The cloned ID wasn't the only thing planted?\"\n\nOutside...\n\nRain began falling over Westbridge once again.\n\nStudents hurried across campus beneath umbrellas.\n\nHigh above them...\n\nSomeone watched from the window of a nearby building.\n\nThe figure quietly closed the curtain.\n\n💭 Ending Quote\n\"The closer the truth comes... the more carefully it hides.\"   🌧️"
