      "title": "An Unexpected Ally",
      "content": "📖 Opening Quote\n\"Not every hero stands in the light. Some quietly guide others toward it.\"\n\nRain tapped gently against the windows of Daniel's office.\n\nThe yellow sticky note lay on his desk.\n\nCheck visitor log again.\n\nHe was certain it hadn't been there before.\n\nSomeone had entered his office...\n\nOr slipped it into the file before he opened it.\n\nEither way...\n\nSomeone knew details of the investigation.\n\nAnd someone wanted him to keep looking.\n\nDaniel returned to the records office.\n\nThis time, he ignored the names.\n\nInstead...\n\nHe studied the times.\n\nEvery visitor who entered after office hours.\n\nEvery authorization stamp.\n\nEvery signature.\n\nThen something caught his attention.\n\nOne entry had been written with blue ink.\n\nEvery other entry that week...\n\nHad been written in black.\n\nA tiny difference.\n\nEasy to overlook.\n\nBut Daniel had learned that the smallest details often mattered most.\n\n\"Has this register ever been rewritten?\" he asked the records clerk.\n\nThe clerk shook his head.\n\n\"Never.\"\n\n\"Each page is filled in on the same day.\"\n\nDaniel pointed at the blue entry.\n\n\"Then why is this one different?\"\n\nThe clerk leaned closer.\n\nHis expression slowly changed.\n\n\"...It shouldn't be.\"\n\nMeanwhile...\n\nThe final examination ended.\n\nStudents streamed out of the lecture halls cheering.\n\nSome hugged each other.\n\nOthers took photos.\n\nMarcus raised both hands.\n\n\"We're free!\"\n\nLena laughed.\n\n\"I thought you'd cry.\"\n\n\"I almost did.\"\n\nEthan smiled.\n\n\"I think we all almost did.\"\n\nAriana looked around the lively campus.\n\nFor a brief moment...\n\nShe forgot about the investigation.\n\nShe was simply another student celebrating the end of exams.\n\nThe Circle of Five gathered beneath the old oak tree one last time before heading home.\n\nMarcus looked around at his friends.\n\n\"We promised we'd meet here after our last exam.\"\n\n\"And we did.\"\n\nLena smiled.\n\n\"No matter where life takes us...\"\n\n\"I hope we never forget this place.\"\n\nChloe looked up at the branches swaying in the breeze.\n\n\"We won't.\"\n\nAriana quietly touched the rough bark of the tree.\n\n\"So many memories...\"\n\n\"So many dreams.\"\n\nEthan smiled.\n\n\"And plenty of embarrassing stories.\"\n\nEveryone laughed.\n\nThe sound echoed across the nearly empty courtyard.\n\nLater that evening...\n\nDaniel received an envelope with no return address.\n\nInside...\n\nWas a photocopy of the missing maintenance file.\n\nRA-218.\n\nHis pulse quickened.\n\nSomeone had found it.\n\nOr...\n\nSomeone had been keeping it hidden.\n\nHe quickly turned the pages.\n\nNear the end of the file...\n\nOne line had been circled in red.\n\nTemporary card reader calibration completed by external contractor.\n\nDaniel frowned.\n\nHe checked the signature.\n\nIt wasn't a name.\n\nJust an employee number.\n\nHe looked up slowly.\n\n\"If I can identify this contractor...\"\n\n\"I may finally know who opened the door for all of this.\"\n\nOutside...\n\nThe rain stopped.\n\nFor the first time in weeks...\n\nA patch of sunlight broke through the clouds.\n\n💭 Ending Quote\n\"Sometimes hope arrives quietly... folded inside an ordinary envelope.\"   🌤️"
