      "content": "📖 Opening Quote\n\"The truth rarely appears all at once. It arrives one honest answer at a time.\"\n\nThe following morning...\n\nDaniel drove to the address listed beside the employee number in the maintenance file.\n\nIt led him to a small electronics company on the outskirts of the city.\n\nThe office manager welcomed him politely.\n\n\"I understand you're looking into work done for Westbridge University.\"\n\nDaniel nodded.\n\n\"I'm trying to identify the technician who serviced a card reader several months ago.\"\n\nThe manager searched through old records.\n\nAfter several minutes...\n\nHe looked up.\n\n\"I found the job.\"\n\nDaniel leaned forward.\n\n\"Who completed it?\"\n\nThe manager frowned.\n\n\"That's strange.\"\n\n\"What is it?\"\n\n\"The technician assigned to the job reported that the repair was canceled before he ever\narrived.\"\n\nDaniel's expression hardened.\n\n\"So he never entered the university?\"\n\n\"No.\"\n\n\"He was paid a cancellation fee and sent to another location.\"\n\nDaniel remained silent.\n\nIf the technician never repaired the card reader...\n\nThen who did?\n\nBack at Westbridge University...\n\nGraduation preparations had begun.\n\nWorkers decorated the main auditorium.\n\nStudents posed for photographs across the campus.\n\nMarcus stretched his arms.\n\n\"I still can't believe we're graduating.\"\n\nLena smiled.\n\n\"It feels unreal.\"\n\nAriana watched students laughing together.\n\nA small smile crossed her face.\n\nFor the first time in weeks...\n\nThe campus looked hopeful again.\n\nThat afternoon...\n\nDaniel met with Professor Adams.\n\nHe laid the maintenance file on the desk.\n\n\"The contractor never came.\"\n\nProfessor Adams looked surprised.\n\n\"Then the repair record is false.\"\n\n\"Exactly.\"\n\n\"Someone wanted the university to believe the card reader had been serviced.\"\n\nProfessor Adams frowned.\n\n\"So the tampering happened without authorization.\"\n\nDaniel nodded.\n\n\"And whoever did it understood the university's systems.\"\n\nMeanwhile...\n\nThe Circle of Five gathered for coffee before heading home for the semester break.\n\nMarcus raised his cup.\n\n\"To surviving university.\"\n\n\"To friendship,\" Lena added.\n\nEthan smiled.\n\n\"To new beginnings.\"\n\nChloe looked around the table.\n\n\"And to never losing touch.\"\n\nAriana lifted her cup last.\n\n\"To truth.\"\n\nThe others looked at her.\n\nShe smiled gently.\n\n\"I don't know how long this investigation will last.\"\n\n\"But I know one day...\"\n\n\"The truth will find all of us.\"\n\nNo one spoke for a moment.\n\nThen they quietly clinked their cups together.\n\nLate that evening...\n\nDaniel returned to his office.\n\nHe spread every document across the desk.\n\nVisitor logs.\n\nMaintenance reports.\n\nCCTV images.\n\nThe cloned ID records.\n\nThe anonymous notes.\n\nThe flash drive.\n\nHe stepped back.\n\nSomething still didn't fit.\n\nEvery piece of evidence pointed to careful planning.\n\nYet...\n\nOne question remained unanswered.\n\nHow had the culprit always known where Ariana would be?\n\nDaniel looked again at a campus map pinned to the wall.\n\nThen his eyes slowly widened.\n\n\"They didn't need to follow her...\"\n\n\"They already knew her routine.\"\n\nThe realization sent a chill through him.\n\nThis wasn't the work of a stranger.\n\nIt was someone who had spent enough time around Ariana to know her habits.\n\nSomeone she trusted.\n\nSomeone who never looked suspicious.\n\nDaniel quietly closed the file.\n\nThe circle of suspects had just become much smaller.\n\n💭 Ending Quote\n          🌙\n\"The deepest betrayals don't come from strangers... they come from the people you never thought to\nquestion.\""
